foundation.question_text:
The weighted network shows connections between four towns $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.5);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,2.5);
\coordinate (C) at (3.2,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$5$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$8$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$4$};
\draw (D) -- (A) node[midway, left] {$6$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$9$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Construct the adjacency matrix for this network.

The directed network shows one-way connections between four servers $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings, mark=at position 0.6 with {\arrow{>}}}, postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (3,2.4);
\coordinate (C) at (3,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$4$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (C) node[pos=0.25, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$8$};
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (D) node[midway, left] {$3$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$6$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (D) node[pos=0.75, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$4$};
\draw[midarrow] (C) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$7$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
Represent this directed network as a table.

development.question_text:
The diagram and incomplete distance table represent four connected towns.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.2);
\coordinate (B) at (3,2.2);
\coordinate (C) at (3,0);
\coordinate (D) at (0,0);
\draw (A) -- (B) node[midway, above] {$11$};
\draw (B) -- (C) node[midway, right] {$14$};
\draw (C) -- (D) node[midway, below] {$8$};
\draw (D) -- (A) node[midway, left] {$19$};
\draw (A) -- (C) node[midway, fill=white, inner sep=1pt] {$16$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt) node[above left] {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt) node[above right] {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt) node[below left] {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{array}{c|cccc} \text{From/To} & A & B & C & D \\ \hline A & - & 11 & 16 & x \\ B & 11 & - & y & - \\ C & 16 & y & - & 8 \\ D & x & - & 8 & - \end{array}$
Determine the values of $x$ and $y$.
